    description: "DECISION REQUESTED, not a defect. Should hypergumbo-tracker and subprocess\ntests be brought into the measured coverage scope?\n\nWHAT IT WOULD BUY, measured 2026-08-14. 3,614 tests (15.9% of the suite)\nproduce no coverage rows at all: hypergumbo-tracker 2,818 (outside COV_PATHS),\nimport-time-subject 435, subprocess 255, scripts/ 106. They cost 12.4 min of\nserial time that NO trajectory can avoid, because a test coverage cannot see\ncan never be selected against -- 57% of the 21.7-min full-coverage trajectory\nis this mandatory floor. hypergumbo-tracker alone is 6.0 min of it.\n\nBringing them in would put that 6 minutes onto the board where selection can\nreach it, and would shrink the unmeasured population that Phase 3 has to\nspecial-case.\n\nWHY IT IS A DECISION AND NOT A TASK: it changes what the repo's 100%-coverage\ngate MEANS. The tracker package is currently tested in isolation with its own\nregime; subprocess coverage needs COVERAGE_PROCESS_START wiring. Both alter\nthe gate's denominator, which is an owner call, not a side effect of tuning a\nselector."  # 3b23
    fields: {}  # 3b23
